## 3. Typography

Avoid the usual suspects (Inter, Roboto, system stacks). We want warmth and editorial confidence.

### Fonts

- **Display / headings**: **Fraunces** — variable serif, set with `opsz` high and slight softness. Alternatives: _Young Serif_, _Recoleta_.
- **Body / UI**: **Nunito** — rounded, friendly, highly readable for tired eyes. Alternatives: _DM Sans_, _Plus Jakarta Sans_.
- **Numerics (weights, times, measurements)**: **Fraunces** at tabular figure setting, or body font with `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`. Numbers should feel like hand-written journal entries, not spreadsheet cells.

### Scale (mobile-first, px)

| Token | Size / Line | Weight | Use |
|---|---|---|---|
| `display` | 40 / 48 | Fraunces 400 | Hero screens, celebrations |
| `h1` | 28 / 36 | Fraunces 500 | Page titles |
| `h2` | 22 / 30 | Fraunces 500 | Section titles |
| `h3` | 18 / 26 | Nunito 700 | Card titles |
| `body-lg` | 17 / 26 | Nunito 400 | Primary reading |
| `body` | 15 / 22 | Nunito 400 | Default UI |
| `caption` | 13 / 18 | Nunito 600 | Labels, metadata |
| `micro` | 11 / 14 | Nunito 700, tracked +40 | Uppercase tags |

### Rules
- Headlines in Fraunces get **-1% letter-spacing**, optical size 48+.
- Body text never goes below 15px on mobile.
- Numerics are always tabular in tables, logs, and stat cards.
- Never bold body text for emphasis — use Fraunces italic or a sage-100 highlight instead.

