## 4. Spacing, Radii, Elevation

### Spacing (8-point, with 4 allowed for tight clusters)
`4 · 8 · 12 · 16 · 24 · 32 · 48 · 64 · 96`

- Screen horizontal padding: 20 mobile, 32 tablet, 64 desktop.
- Card internal padding: 20.
- Vertical rhythm between sections: 32 mobile, 48 desktop.

### Radii
- `--r-sm`: 8 (chips, tags)
- `--r-md`: 14 (inputs, small buttons)
- `--r-lg`: 20 (cards, modals)
- `--r-xl`: 28 (hero surfaces, bottom sheets)
- `--r-pill`: 999 (avatars, primary CTAs)

Never use perfectly square corners. Never use radii above 32 except for circular elements.

### Elevation (soft, warm shadows — never grey)

```css
--shadow-sm:  0 1px 2px rgba(80, 70, 50, 0.06);
--shadow-md:  0 4px 12px rgba(80, 70, 50, 0.08);
--shadow-lg:  0 12px 32px rgba(80, 70, 50, 0.10);
--shadow-focus: 0 0 0 3px rgba(156, 165, 122, 0.35); /* sage glow */
```

Elevation is used _sparingly_. Most cards are defined by a 1px `--linen-200` border, not a shadow. Shadows appear on floating elements only (FAB, modals, toasts, active popovers).

### Texture
A nearly-invisible paper grain on `--linen-50` background (SVG noise at 3% opacity) gives the whole app a tactile, journal-like quality. This is optional but elevates the aesthetic significantly.

