## 7. Content Patterns (the baby-specific screens)

### Daily timeline
The default screen. A vertical timeline with **time on the left rail** in Fraunces tabular, event cards on the right. Events grouped by morning / afternoon / evening / night with small botanical dividers between.

Each event card shows icon + label + one key metric. Tap to expand for full notes, photos, duration.

### Growth tracker
Weight, height, head circumference. Rendered as a soft-curve line chart (no grid lines, no axis ticks — just the curve, two endpoint dots, and the WHO percentile band as a translucent sage shape behind it). Hover/tap a point reveals the measurement in a Fraunces-numbered card.

### Food & allergy log
Two-column structure: **Tried** and **Reactions**. Each food is a chip. Allergens auto-promote from Tried to a dedicated Allergies watchlist at the top of the page, flagged with `--clay`. Severity levels (mild / moderate / severe) use dot indicators, never stars.

### Milestones
A scrolling list of cards, each with its illustration, date achieved, and a short parent-written note. Completed milestones show a quiet peach checkmark in the corner, not a full celebration — the celebration happens _in the moment_ of logging, not permanently.

### Notes / journal
Rich-text but minimal: bold, italic, bullet, photo inline, voice memo. No headings, no tables — this is a journal, not a wiki. Each note has a sage leaf bullet on the left margin to signify it's a "planted" thought.

### Quick log sheet
Bottom sheet with 4 big buttons (Feed, Sleep, Diaper, Other), each 80px tall, icon + label. Selecting one opens a second sheet with minimal required fields and a big "Log" button. Should take under 5 seconds start to finish.

